# Line endings.
#
# Git stores text blobs as LF, but without this file each machine's
# core.autocrlf decides what lands in the working tree. On Windows that means
# CRLF on disk, which (a) makes `npm run format:check` fail on every file,
# since Prettier's default endOfLine is "lf", and (b) makes the same file look
# 100% changed when diffed against a checkout from another platform — which
# turns every `git merge upstream/master` review into noise.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree to LF everywhere, matching CI and Prettier.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets. Never line-ending-normalize or textually diff these —
# misdetecting one as text corrupts it.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.webm  binary

# SVG is text — keep it diffable.
*.svg   text eol=lf

# Generated: collapse in GitHub diffs so it does not drown out real review.
package-lock.json linguist-generated
